      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing S3 for Implementation**\n\nI've decided to use Amazon S3 as the managed object storage provider. The Python file, `object_metadata.py`, will leverage the `boto3` library. This is a practical choice given its widespread adoption and strong community support. The immediate next step is to start writing code using `boto3` for object metadata retrieval.\n\n\n**Defining Metadata Retrieval Logic**\n\nI'm now solidifying the architecture for `object_metadata.py`. The core will be a function, `get_object_metadata`, accepting `bucket_name` and `object_key` as arguments. This function will employ `boto3` to interact with S3. The design will use the `head_object` method to grab the metadata, then return it. My focus is on writing the code now.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819501362,
          "start": 1789819499779
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98e3503001UmjQGdI2swd8eP",
