      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Code's Purpose**\n\nI'm starting to build a Python script, aiming for `presigned_download.py`, that will produce time-limited download URLs. I'm focusing on incorporating a specific object storage provider into the code. The objective is clear: to generate pre-signed URLs for secure, temporary access to stored objects, and so need to define the method to use.\n\n\n**Implementing the Download Script**\n\nI've begun building the Python script, `presigned_download.py`, and am now working to integrate AWS S3 using `boto3`. I have defined the function `create_presigned_download_url` that will handle URL generation. This function will accept the bucket name, object name, and expiration time as inputs. I'm focusing on ensuring `boto3` and the AWS S3 client are explicitly used to create the time-limited URLs.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819496752,
          "start": 1789819494853
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98e21c5001fJB05GsdWMjRiR",
      "message_id": "msg_0b98e1c76001YbGNfBHryHK2ZZ",
      "session_id": "ses_f4671e397ffeKlOD7L9Er3AkPN",
      "time_created": 1789819494853,
      "time_updated": 1789819496753
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "2kIGEH80XwIeVnBR",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef create_presigned_download_url(bucket_name: str, object_name: str, expiration: int = 3600):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate a presigned URL to download an S3 object.\n\n    :param bucket_name: Name of the S3 bucket\n    :param object_name: Key of the S3 object\n    :param expiration: Time in seconds for the presigned URL to remain valid. Defaults to 3600 seconds (1 hour).\n    :return: Presigned URL as string. If error, returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    s3_client = boto3.client('s3')\n    try:\n        response = s3_client.generate_presigned_url('get_object',\n                                                    Params={'Bucket': bucket_name,\n                                                            'Key': object_name},\n                                                    ExpiresIn=expiration)\n    except ClientError as e:\n        print(f\"Error generating presigned URL: {e}\")\n        return None\n    return response\n\n",
            "filePath": "presigned_download.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
