      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Object Storage Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with AWS S3 as the object storage solution. Now, I am planning to implement the file upload functionality in Python, I intend to use the `boto3` library for interacting with the S3 service. I need to make sure the code clearly indicates AWS S3 is being used.\n\n\n**Confirming S3 Implementation**\n\nI've confirmed using AWS S3 with `boto3`. I'm focused on `upload_object.py`. The plan includes functions for both file and byte stream uploads to the S3 bucket. The code will initialize the AWS S3 client, making the specific provider clear.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819492435,
          "start": 1789819489919
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b98e0e7f001bIhO09UMU6gm5v",
      "message_id": "msg_0b98e07c3001U5ldzvp6YI2OGI",
      "session_id": "ses_f4671f8c5ffeHXgjKptIGbeTKJ",
      "time_created": 1789819489919,
